---
const rungs = [
  {
    label: "Off-the-shelf builder",
    sub: "Wix, Squarespace, CompanyCam, Houzz Pro",
    body: "He could edit it himself, but they template the look (the one thing he asked me not to do) and bill monthly, anywhere from $16 to $399. Even the polished ones make him a tenant on someone else's platform.",
    transition:
      "So I built custom. That fixed the look and the cost. Now the real question: how does he add a photo after every job?",
    shipped: false,
  },
  {
    label: "Hand him the CMS's own studio",
    sub: "A headless CMS as his editor",
    body: "A headless CMS lets him post without touching code, and runs on a free tier. But its studio is built for a developer, not for a guy posting one-handed on his phone in his second language. And his phone is the only way he was ever going to post. Too clunky to be his.",
    transition: "So I built one more layer.",
    shipped: false,
  },
  {
    label: "A Spanish upload page on top",
    sub: "What's live",
    body: "One screen, a few fields, as easy as posting to Instagram. His own custom look, no monthly subscription, and finally something he'd actually use.",
    transition: null,
    shipped: true,
  },
];
---

<!-- Why I Built Instead of Bought -->
<section class="mb-24">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-2">Build vs Buy</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg mb-10">
    <p>
      He was clear from the start: he wanted a site that felt like his, not a
      template like every other contractor in town. So the look wasn't a
      nice-to-have, it was the brief.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="max-w-3xl">
    {
      rungs.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <div
            class:list={[
              "rounded-2xl border p-6 shadow-sm",
              r.shipped
                ? "border-violet-200 bg-gradient-to-br from-violet-50 to-white"
                : "border-gray-200 bg-white",
            ]}
          >
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
              <h3
                class:list={[
                  "font-semibold text-lg",
                  r.shipped ? "text-violet-900" : "text-gray-900",
                ]}
              >
                {r.label}
              </h3>
              <span
                class:list={[
                  "text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 border",
                  r.shipped
                    ? "text-violet-700 bg-violet-100 border-violet-200"
                    : "text-gray-500 bg-gray-50 border-gray-200",
                ]}
              >
                {r.sub}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p
              class:list={[
                "text-sm leading-relaxed",
                r.shipped ? "text-gray-700" : "text-gray-600",
              ]}
            >
              {r.body}
            </p>
          </div>

          {r.transition && (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2 py-4 pl-1">
              <svg
                class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-amber-500"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"
                />
              </svg>
              <span class="text-sm font-medium leading-relaxed text-amber-800">
                {r.transition}
              </span>
            </div>
          )}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
    For a contractor who's comfortable with tech and fine paying monthly, I'd
    have set him up on Squarespace and saved myself two rungs. He's not that
    guy, so I climbed them.
  </p>
</section>
